ng trees and falls back to the current checkout, which is the defect this change exists to fix. Fix: in `test_a_later_boundary_review_is_compared`, also read `blind-sheet.json` and assert that the re-raise item's `repo`/`base_tree`/`head_tree` match the later review's native event (they must be real trees, as in the end-to-end tree test). Check it goes red with the lookup removed.", "files": ["tests/test_native_review_compare.py"], "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 1, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "README step 2 still describes the old per-instrument questions", "recommendation": "Records Pass over files_oracle (blind-sheet.md, README.md, compare.py): .prawduct/research/native-review-paired/README.md step 2 still says the sheet asks \"real defect?\" for a unique finding and asks which goal only for a native-only finding. That is false now: compare.py asks every unique finding UNIQUE_ASK. It clears no bar, because the verifier answers the `ask` printed on the sheet, so this is not a finding. If the sentence is touched, make it relational (\"answer each item's `ask`\") and say in step 3 that the verifier's goal answer counts only for native-only findings, since a Critic finding's goal is in its fact. The change record's claims (one question, shuffled order with `first` in the key, trees from the native.review event) check out against compare.py and native_review.record.", "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "A re-raise item names only the later review's trees", "recommendation": "A re-raise item's `earlier` findings were raised against an earlier review's trees, but the item carries only the later review's `base_tree`/`head_tree`. A verifier that wants to check \"same defect?\" against the earlier code has no tree to read it at. This is fine if the words are enough to judge it; otherwise attach `where()` of the earlier review to each `earlier` entry, using the key's `earlier_review` to look it up.", "oid": "O-2"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `fix/blind-sheet`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "27660e70a04bbcbfebf78516548238e0606fffbb", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/changes/blind-sheet.md", ".prawduct/research/native-review-paired/README.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "span": "full", "bounded_from": null, "span_reason": "no-boundary-review", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-14T19:11:37Z"}}

